  "title": "The Downeaster Alexa",
  "artist": "Billy Joel",
  "genre": "unknown",
  "original_lyrics": "[verse]\nWell I'm on the Downeaster Alexa\nAnd I'm cruising through Block Island Sound.\nI have chartered course to the Vineyard.\n\n[bridge]\nWe took on diesel back in Montauk yesterday,\nAnd left this morning from the bell in Gardiner's Bay.\nLike all the locals here I've had to sell my home,\nToo proud to leave, I worked my fingers to the bone\nSo I could own my Downeaster Alexa,\nAnd I go where the ocean is deep.\nThere are giants out there in the canyons.\nAnd good captain can't fall asleep.\nI got bills to pay and children who need clothes.\nI know there's fish out there but where, God only knows.\nThey say these waters aren't what they used to be.\n\n[bridge]\nSo when you see my Downeaster Alexa,\nAnd if you work with the rod and the reel,\nTell my wife I trolling Atlantis,\nAnd I still have my hands on the wheel.\nNow I drive my Downeaster Alexa\nMore and more miles from shore ev'ry year,\nSince they told me I can't sell no stripers.\nAnd there's no luck in sword fishing here.\nI was bayman like my father was before.\n\n[chorus]\nThere ain't much future for man who works the sea.\n\n[bridge]\nYa, ya, ya yo\nYa, ya, ya yo\nYa, ya, ya yo\nYa, ya, ya yo",
